From: Rafael Bernardy <rafaelbernardyd>
Date: Wed, 09 Jul 2026 11:30:23 +0000
Subject: cursor-renderer: Make software cursor overlay visibility per-view

The software cursor overlay's visibility was tracked as a single
flag shared by the whole stage, computed by OR-ing hardware-cursor
support across every view. As soon as any view had a hardware
cursor, the overlay was hidden everywhere, including on views that
have no hardware cursor plane at all and need the software fallback.

This breaks the cursor on views that lack hardware cursor support
while another view on the same stage has it, e.g. on Q8B SC8280XP
with 3 displays but only 2 hardware cursor planes: the display
without a cursor plane gets no cursor because the global flag hides
the software overlay as soon as another display uses hardware cursor.

MetaOverlay already tracks per-view state (used for redraw
clipping), and MetaOverlay's paint function already receives the
ClutterStageView being painted. Extend that per-view state to also
track hardware-cursor availability, and consult it in
meta_overlay_paint() and queue_redraw_for_cursor_overlay() instead
of the global visibility flag alone. The native cursor renderer
already computes hardware-cursor support per view; feed that
directly into the overlay per view instead of collapsing it into a
single OR'd value.

Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/5172
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/work_items/4897
Bug-Radxa: Q8B 三屏扩展模式第三个屏幕（无硬件 cursor plane）鼠标光标消失
Forwarded: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/5172
Last-Update: 2026-07-22
diff --git a/src/backends/meta-cursor-renderer.c b/src/backends/meta-cursor-renderer.c
index 3ccd48c8b..e6ff84d2e 100644
--- a/src/backends/meta-cursor-renderer.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-cursor-renderer.c
@@ -142,9 +142,6 @@ meta_cursor_renderer_update_stage_overlay (MetaCursorRenderer *renderer,
 
   g_set_object (&priv->overlay_cursor, cursor);
 
-  if (!priv->stage_overlay)
-    priv->stage_overlay = meta_stage_create_cursor_overlay (META_STAGE (stage));
-
   graphene_matrix_init_identity (&matrix);
   if (cursor)
     {
@@ -302,6 +299,8 @@ meta_cursor_renderer_constructed (GObject *object)
                       G_CALLBACK (meta_cursor_renderer_after_paint),
                       renderer);
 
+  priv->stage_overlay = meta_stage_create_cursor_overlay (META_STAGE (stage));
+
   G_OBJECT_CLASS (meta_cursor_renderer_parent_class)->constructed (object);
 }
 
@@ -608,3 +607,12 @@ meta_cursor_renderer_needs_overlay (MetaCursorRenderer *renderer)
 
   return priv->needs_overlay;
 }
+
+MetaOverlay *
+meta_cursor_renderer_get_stage_overlay (MetaCursorRenderer *renderer)
+{
+  MetaCursorRendererPrivate *priv =
+    meta_cursor_renderer_get_instance_private (renderer);
+
+  return priv->stage_overlay;
+}
